{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "What a resource pack may change. A pack is data read by code already in the build (the update center's L2 layer), so it can only replace copy and colours that exist and add emoji; it never adds behaviour. The four kits run this table against their own rules (Vue `flareResource*`, Flutter, SwiftUI and Compose `flareResource*` and `FlareResourceOverlay`); strings keys are the kit's own vocabulary, so the table uses made-up keys and each kit tests its real fields on its own.",
  "rules": {
    "content": "A pack's `contentJson` is a JSON object whose `schema` is `flare.resource.v1` and whose `kind` equals the pack's. Anything else ignores the whole pack, without an error. A `help` pack parses but the kit has nothing to fold it into: the host reads its `contentJson`.",
    "placeholders": "`{name}` (letters, digits, underscore), `%s`, `%d` and `%@`, as a set: order and repeats do not count.",
    "strings": "An entry is kept when its key has a built-in plain string, its value is a string that is not blank, and its placeholders equal the built-in value's. A value is kept as written. An entry that fails is ignored; the others stand. A field that is a function has no built-in plain string, so it cannot be replaced.",
    "locales": "Tags compare without case, with `_` read as `-`. Exact first, then the requested tag cut one subtag at a time, then the first tag in sorted order that extends the requested one. No match means the pack says nothing for this language: copy never crosses into another language.",
    "colors": "Only the groups `colors` (light) and `dark` (dark) exist; neither falls back to the other, so a light value never reaches the dark theme. A key must be a known colour and a value `#RRGGBB` or `#RRGGBBAA`. Sizes, spacing and type are not open: their groups are not read.",
    "argb": "A colour for the native kits: `#RRGGBB` is opaque, `#RRGGBBAA` puts its alpha first. Vue writes the value as it is.",
    "emoji": "Only adds. A pack entry needs a safe `id` that no built-in or earlier pack has and a title that is not blank. A sticker needs a safe `stickerId` new to its pack and a `url`; an emoji needs a `key` no built-in or earlier entry has and a `url`. Every image address must be https, and one that is not ignores the entry it sits on. Optional fields that are null or blank are left out. A pack left with nothing is dropped; a pack with emoji and no stickers adds no sticker tab.",
    "fold": "Packs apply in the order given, which the engine sorts by id: the later pack wins a key. Each pack is judged against the built-in value, never against an earlier pack."
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "a matching pack parses",
      "kind": "strings",
      "contentJson": "{\"schema\": \"flare.resource.v1\", \"kind\": \"strings\", \"locales\": {}}",
      "accepted": true
    },
    {
      "name": "a help pack parses",
      "kind": "help",
      "contentJson": "{\"schema\": \"flare.resource.v1\", \"kind\": \"help\", \"articles\": []}",
      "accepted": true
    },
    {
      "name": "broken JSON is ignored",
      "kind": "strings",
      "contentJson": "{\"schema\":",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "an empty string is ignored",
      "kind": "strings",
      "contentJson": "",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "a root that is not an object is ignored",
      "kind": "strings",
      "contentJson": "[]",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "a missing schema is ignored",
      "kind": "strings",
      "contentJson": "{\"kind\": \"strings\"}",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "another schema version is ignored",
      "kind": "strings",
      "contentJson": "{\"schema\": \"flare.resource.v2\", \"kind\": \"strings\"}",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "a kind that disagrees with the manifest is ignored",
      "kind": "tokens",
      "contentJson": "{\"schema\": \"flare.resource.v1\", \"kind\": \"strings\"}",
      "accepted": false
    }
  ],
